  "query_preview": "..\n/Issued 1230 AM MST Sat Nov 7 2026/ \n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nThis morning, an upper level trough to the North of MT moves east\nas ridging aloft builds to the west. This results in strong winds\nacross the Northern Rocky Mountain Front and High Plains through \nmid-day. By the afternoon, the axis of the upper level ridge will \nbe close to centered over MT, allowing for a lull in the strong \nwinds through tomorrow morning. \n\nOn Sunday, the upper-level ridge breaks down. This, combined with\nstrong low-level and mid-level winds, will bring another day of \nwindy conditions to North-Central Montana. The strongest winds \nwill be along the Rocky Mountain Front with an extension of \nstrongest winds from favorable mountain wave effects downrange \nover the northern plains west of I-15. On Monday, an upper-level \nridge moves back over North-Central, Central, and Southwestern \nMontana. This will continue the warm and dry conditions for the \narea. Tuesday through Thursday, the upper-level ridge remains over\nNorth-central Montana. This will keep warm and dry weather for \nthe area Tuesday through Thursday, with breezy winds. -IG/RA\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nOn Sunday along the Hi-line east of I-15 and in the lower-elevations \nof Cascade County there is a 30 - 70% chance for wind gusts of 55 \nmph or greater. On Sunday along the Rocky Mountain Front there is a \n40 - 70% chance for wind gusts of 80 mph or greater. On Sunday \nacross the plains west of I-15 there is a 50 - 90% chance for wind \ngusts of 70 mph or greater. As a result during the day on Sunday the \nHigh Wind Watch for Glacier County, Western Toole County, Pondera \nCounty, and the Rocky Mountain Front of Teton and Lewis and Clark Co \nhas been upgraded to a High Wind Warning. Eastern Toole, Liberty, \nHill, and Cascade County remain in a High Wind Watch. -IG/RA",
